   "properties": {
    "lc_note": {
     "source": "en",
     "texts": {
      "en": {
       "text": "## LC Krea2 LoRA Editor\n\n### 🛑🚫✋ Read this first\n- 🧪 **BETA, still in testing.** Presets and defaults can change between versions. Keep your original LoRA files.\n- Krea 2 LoRAs only (for now). ZIT and Klein come later.\n- **Block Scan** renders 64 images (8 rows x 8 seeds). About 7 minutes on a 5090. It only runs again when you change its settings, so tweak the Editor all you want after the first run.\n- Use a prompt with one clear face. The scan needs a face to score.\n- The face models download once (InsightFace buffalo_l, non-commercial license) and need **onnxruntime**.\n\n**LC Krea2 LoRA Block Scan**\n- Renders the same seeds with no LoRA, with the full LoRA, then with the LoRA turned off in one block group at a time.\n- **same face**: how alike the faces are across the seeds. Lower = more variety.\n\n| Score | What it looks like |\n|---|---|\n| 0.0 - 0.2 | Clearly different people |\n| 0.2 - 0.35 | Different people who share a few features |\n| 0.35 - 0.5 | Could be sisters |\n| 0.5 - 1.0 | Same person |\n\n- **vs base**: how far the render moved from the model without the LoRA (LPIPS, 0 = identical). A LoRA meant to change one thing should keep this low.\n- **vs LoRA**: how much of the LoRA's look you lose with that group off.\n- **blocks**: the suggested curve. The group that frees the face most drops to 0.3. If nothing beats the seed noise (0.03), it stays all 1 and the report says so.\n- 💡 Face lock hides in different blocks for every LoRA (Lip Bite: 16-21, Amateur V4: 4-9). That is the whole reason this node exists.\n\n**LC Krea2 LoRA Editor**\n- Sits where a LoRA loader would. Model in, model out.\n- **blocks_in** is wired to the scan. Unplug it to drag the bars yourself (0 to 2, double-click resets a bar).\n- **preset**: block groups to try by hand. **Tame** = blocks 4-15 at 0.7.\n- **attention / mlp / outside_blocks**: scale those layers in every block at once.\n- **spike_soften**: **directions** flattens the one direction that dominates a layer. This is what stopped Lip Bite from changing the whole image. **spike_limit** 2 is a good start.\n- The heatmap shows each layer's strength before and after, filled in after a run.\n\n**LC Face Variety Scorer 🧑‍🤝‍🧑**\n- Scores the Editor's test batch (same seeds as the scan), so you can check the fix without running the scan again.\n\n**LC LoRA Save**\n- ⚠️ Muted. NOTHING SAVES UNLESS IT IS TURNED ON! (Ctrl+M)\n- Saves to **models/loras** with every edit baked in. Loads at 1.0 in any LoRA loader.\n- **rank**: 0 keeps it. Any other number makes a smaller file.\n\n---"
      }
     },
     "titles": {}
    }
   },
